    <string name="readme_h_glossary">What the words mean</string>
    <string name="readme_gloss_build">**build**: one day. It passes when everything due got done, it is **unstable** when some of it did, it fails when none of it did. The numbers are always printed beside the word.</string>
    <string name="readme_gloss_commit">**commit**: the entry a closed day leaves in the history. A day you never opened the app leaves none, because nothing is known about it.</string>
    <string name="readme_gloss_health">**health**: how often a habit has held lately, as a percentage. Recent days count for more than old ones, and days you skipped or never opened the app do not count at all.</string>
    <string name="readme_gloss_coverage">**coverage**: how many of the days that asked something of you were days you actually opened the app. It measures you showing up, not you succeeding.</string>
    <string name="readme_gloss_flaky">**flaky**: a habit you manage about half the time. It is not a scolding: usually it means the habit is asking for too much, or asking on the wrong days.</string>
    <string name="readme_gloss_regression">**regression**: a habit that used to hold and lately does not. It is said once, without advice.</string>
