    <!-- The `amend` entry names a git flag whose two hyphens are part of the
         command: an em dash there would be a command that does not exist. -->
    <string-array name="help_md" tools:ignore="TypographyDashes">
        <item># thabit</item>
        <item></item>
        <item>A habit tracker that presents itself as a code editor and a test suite: your habits are a checklist, a day is a run of it, and the past is a history you can read. If the words below mean nothing to you, this page is for you.</item>
        <item></item>
        <item>## The four tabs</item>
        <item></item>
        <item>- **Editor** - `habits.test` and `README.md`: today. The first is the checklist you tick off; the second is the same day told in words.</item>
        <item>- **Log** - `habits_history.diff`: one entry per closed day, saying what you did and what you did not.</item>
        <item>- **Stats** - `stats.md`: the coloured grid of the last weeks (one square per day) and a table with a row per habit.</item>
        <item>- **Settings** - `settings.config` and this file. Options change by tapping the value itself. There is no switch to hunt for.</item>
        <item></item>
        <item>## The borrowed words</item>
        <item></item>
        <item>- **test** - one habit. The app calls it a test because a habit, like a test, is something that either held that day or did not.</item>
        <item>- **suite** - all of them together, which is what `habits.test` lists.</item>
        <item>- **assert** - what a habit asks of you: twenty pages, ten minutes, or simply that you did it.</item>
        <item>- **the boxes** - `[ ]` still to do, `[x]` done, `[·]` a habit you are avoiding, still holding, `[~]` skipped on purpose, `[!]` failed. Tapping the box is how you answer.</item>
        <item>- **commit** - a day, closed and filed when the day ends. A committed day stops changing.</item>
        <item>- **`--amend`** - correcting yesterday, which is the one closed day still open to you. The history says where it happened.</item>
        <item>- **diff** - what a day contained, written as changes: `+` for what held, `-` for what did not.</item>
        <item>- **branch** (`⎇`) - what you are looking at.</item>
        <item></item>
        <item>The other words the app prints - `build`, `health`, `coverage`, `flaky`, `regression` - are explained in the `README.md` tab, next to the numbers they are about.</item>
        <item></item>
        <item>## Where the numbers come from</item>
        <item></item>
        <item>From the boxes you tick, and from nothing else. thabit has no network permission at all, no account and no sensors: nothing can leave the phone, because there is nowhere for it to go. Every figure is worked out from your own answers at the moment it is shown, never stored, so correcting a day corrects everything that day was part of. And a day you never opened the app is not counted as a failure: it stays blank, because the app does not know what happened, and it says so.</item>
        <item></item>
        <item>## Why it looks like this</item>
